{%- comment -%}
  The "just landed" card, rendered twice on the home page with a
  different product each time: Click-Key Blocks in the #new band under
  the hero, Sushi Blocks again just above the endless bubble band. One
  source rather than two copies that drift apart the first time the
  layout changes.

  Everything that differs between the two comes in as a parameter --
  handle, title, cta, copy and the fallback photo -- so the snippet
  knows the shape of the card and nothing about either product. The
  product itself is looked up here from the handle rather than passed
  in, because a snippet cannot see variables assigned by the section:
  p_ckb does not cross the render boundary. Global objects do, which is
  what all_products is. This is the same arrangement
  snippets/wt-bubble.liquid uses.

  The caller passes section.settings for copy and fallback_image, which
  keeps both of those editable per band in the theme editor and keeps
  this file from knowing which setting belongs to which product.
{%- endcomment -%}
{% assign new_product = all_products[handle] %}
<article class="wt-new__card">
  <div class="wt-new__media">{% if new_product.featured_image %}<img src="{{ new_product.featured_image | image_url: width: 800 }}" width="{{ new_product.featured_image.width }}" height="{{ new_product.featured_image.height }}" alt="{{ new_product.title }}" class="wt-new__img">{% else %}{% render 'wt-img', img: fallback_image, label: fallback_label, fit: 'contain' %}{% endif %}</div>
  <div class="wt-new__body">
    {%- comment -%}
      "available now" is read off the product rather than written into
      the eyebrow, because the band sits next to a Shop button and the
      two have to agree. A sold-out or unstocked product says "coming
      soon" instead, which is the word the flavour cards in #flavour
      already use for something that is not buyable yet.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <p class="wt-new__eyebrow">Just landed &middot; {% if new_product.available %}available now{% else %}coming soon{% endif %}</p>
    <h2 class="wt-new__title">{{ title }}</h2>
    <p class="wt-new__copy">{{ copy }}</p>
  </div>
  <div class="wt-new__buy">
    <span class="wt-new__price">{{ new_product.price | money_without_trailing_zeros }}</span>
    <a href="{{ new_product.url }}" class="wt-btn wt-btn--nowrap">{{ cta }}</a>
  </div>
</article>
